commit 8af2ae3b88fd68bf3145d74159df307ab8b67c91
Author: Peter Svensson <psvensson@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jun 15 18:49:04 2026 +0200

    fix(cdc): wire anti-entropy sweep into owner-authoritative catch-up (part 1b)
    
    Heals a genuinely-lost CDC DELETE in production: hydrateCdcPropagatedTablesFromAuthority
    now, after the UPSERT-only catch-up read, evicts cache-only rows absent from the
    complete authoritative set (reconcileAgainstAuthoritativeTruth).
    
    Safety: the sweep runs ONLY when the read came from the authoritative OWNER
    (readResult.source === OWNER_RPC_LANE), structurally excluding local-replica reads
    — a lagging follower returning a stale/empty success read must never drive
    eviction. A new evictOlderThanMs race-guard preserves rows written after the read
    snapshot. Sweep keys are derived exactly as the cache stores them.
    
    Distributed rolling-restart stat-gate: 5/5 CONVERGED, missing=0, hardBreaches=0,
    0 corrupt, 0 stale-source — no convergence regression. In-process delete-resurrection
    gate green (0/114). Verified by an adversarial subagent that caught and drove the
    owner-source safety gate.
    
    Coverage boundary (follow-up): catch-up is one-shot at join/recovery, so a stable
    long-lived node won't re-sweep; a periodic owner-rate-limited sweep is deferred to
    avoid added owner load during formation backpressure.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

